## Contract

Every agent definition states:

- one responsibility and its neighboring-role boundaries;
- required approved inputs;
- one fixed deliverable;
- minimum tools and write level;
- prohibited actions;
- evidence and acceptance criteria;
- stop condition and blocker behavior;
- independent second-voice rule;
- human approval gate;
- defect return target and next role.

## Machine-readable contract

`agent-platform/agent-contracts.yml` is the canonical machine projection for the fixed eight-role engineering set. For every role it declares the source agent file, single responsibility, allowed tools, forbidden action classes, provider eligibility and routing strategy, context/output/turn budgets, required input fields, output sections, handoff destinations, data-classification limit, approval requirements, deterministic tests, and live-eval scenarios.

`npm run agents:validate` checks the manifest schema, the fixed role set, reference integrity, policy catalogs, budgets, handoff graph, and drift from `.claude/agents/*.md` frontmatter. The manifest makes contract drift blocking; it does not yet execute providers or replace the planned deterministic pre-tool policy gateway.

Read-only is the default. Implementation write permission is limited to an isolated worktree in the target architecture. The current simulation grants no repository write action to a provider.
